<SimCheck />

<PracticeSet />

<AtTheTable>

On the flop, a missed turn changes the river denominator. Recount on the turn rather than carrying a two-card number into a one-card decision. A probability tree also keeps “hit at least once” separate from “hit twice.”

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>

Sequential forecasts need conditional branches when observations change what can happen next. Multiplying unchanged probabilities is justified only when the relevant dependence has been ruled out. A small tree makes that assumption visible.

</QuantCorner>
